<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Id>EzDbCodeGen</Id>
    <Version>8.3.2</Version>
    <MinClientVersion>8.3.2</MinClientVersion>
    <Title>EzDbCodeGen - Easy Database Code Generator</Title>
    <Authors>Ricardo Vega Jr.</Authors>
    <Owners>Ricardo Vega Jr.</Owners>
    <PackageLicense>https://github.com/rvegajr/ez-db-codegen-core/blob/master/LICENSE</PackageLicense>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/rvegajr/ez-db-codegen-core</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/rvegajr/ez-db-codegen-core</RepositoryUrl>
    <Description>This will install a local cli tool. From this path, you can run a powershell script that will generate code based on the connection string. Each template is a handlebars template that has tags that specify where you would like to output the generated code and if there is a vs project that you wish to update with the file list (old VS project formats only).</Description>
    <Tags>Code-Generation Code-Generator Database Schema</Tags>
    <Summary>A class library that will generate code based on a schema representation in a simple object hierarchy (given by EzDbSchema) and handlebars template(s).</Summary>
    <Copyright>Noctusoft 2018-2024</Copyright>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>


</Project>